 "text": "On December ninth the engineers hauled the bridge sections down the road on trucks. They laid the steel across the gap. The span was barely wide enough. Tanks could ride on the two steel treadways. Jeeps needed wooden panels laid between them. One wrong move and a vehicle would tumble into the gorge below.",
